Subject: Repair CMake exports and bounded process-I/O/move behavior
Applies-to: official cpp-subprocess v2.5
Source: https://github.com/arun11299/cpp-subprocess/commit/60d4ad8d528173a2e4c98fd64aa9191728832355
Source-archive-SHA256: f2c947e0dcfd800652275d6f7deb76d155a953a1a5df969383530445f01c29eb
SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
Upstream-status: not-submitted; downstream package-local corrections
Scope: General build/interface and POSIX boundary corrections, not an ISA feature.
Reason: Fix installed CMake paths/version exports, retain the original piping
 fixture, reject empty commands safely, join empty/multibyte-separator vectors,
 bound startup errors and integer read sizes, consume complete stderr-only
 output, propagate threaded read errors and rebind moved stream ownership.
Tests: Retain all ten original CTests with assertions enabled; add ten exact
 owned consumer groups including long stderr/error, moved streams and EBADF.
Limitations: Static diagnosis only until target CI; not a CVE, exploit,
 performance, universal process-security, or Windows-platform validation claim.
Remove-when: An official release provides equivalent behavior and passes all
 original ten CTests plus the additive installed header/CMake consumers.

